1. A method for positioning and sawing a metal workpiece using a sawing machine having a bench, a plurality of clamping jaws, an upper saw, and a controller, the method comprising:

placing the metal workpiece on the bench between the plurality of clamping jaws;

receiving, by the controller, an offset value representing a distance between a reference position associated with the metal workpiece and a desired cutting position;

causing, by the controller and based on the offset value, relative movement between the metal workpiece and the upper saw to align the desired cutting position with a cutting plane of the upper saw;

actuating the plurality of clamping jaws to secure the metal workpiece in the aligned position;

moving the upper saw downward toward the bench while driving a saw blade of the upper saw; and

cutting the metal workpiece at the desired cutting position with the saw blade.

A method for operating a sawing machine, comprising:

(a) clamping a workpiece between a pair of jaws disposed at an initial position;

(b) inputting, into a controller of the sawing machine, an offset of the workpiece relative to a predetermined zero reference;

(c) aligning a front end of the workpiece with a cutting plane of a saw blade;

(d) releasing the workpiece and resetting the jaws to the initial position;

(e) re-clamping the workpiece between the jaws; and

(f) feeding the re-clamped workpiece toward the saw blade for cutting.

1. **A method of referencing a workpiece in an upper-saw machine having a saw blade disposed above a workpiece support and defining a cutting plane, the method comprising:**  
   positioning a controllable jaw at an initial jaw position and actuating the controllable jaw to clamp the workpiece;  
   receiving an input specifying an offset associated with a reference location of the workpiece;  
   while the workpiece is clamped, moving the controllable jaw selectively in a forward direction or a reverse direction, based on the offset, to align the reference location with the cutting plane;  
   releasing the workpiece after the reference location is aligned with the cutting plane;  
   returning the controllable jaw to the initial jaw position;  
   re-clamping the workpiece with the controllable jaw; and  
   moving the re-clamped workpiece from the referenced position to a cutting position relative to the cutting plane.
